Description:
    Writes a built-in block type of this repository: its definition in
    app/models/block_types (one translated :text field, its theme methods,
    its stylesheet and a sample), its line in config/initializers/types.rb,
    its public component and template in app/components/blocks, its
    stylesheet in the default theme's folder (colours as --th- tokens only),
    an empty scope for its words under public.blocks and under the tile's
    types (each below its marker line; a file without the marker gets
    nothing, and the generator says so), a Lookbook preview built from the
    sample, and two tests. An owner/name type is an engine's, and its
    generator is not built yet (block types spec, step 2).

    A name is refused when it is no lowercase words joined by underscores,
    does not come back from its class name, is read by YAML as true, false
    or nil, is a constant of the application (Post, Tag, Blocks: the
    type's module would shadow it inside module BlockTypes), is a block
    type already, is a stylesheet of the default theme (tokens, prose), or
    when any file it would write exists.

    destroy removes the files and the three lines, and only for a type whose
    definition (and stylesheet) still carry the line "Written by bin/rails
    generate block_type": a built-in, a stylesheet of the default theme or
    a type whose line was taken out is refused, and nothing is removed. A
    scope that has been filled is not "<name>: {}" any more and stays in its
    locale file.

Example:
    bin/rails generate block_type callout
    bin/rails destroy block_type callout
